 * hotfix — development only) — the approved change to files the DEV-UI-01.7, ACC-01, LCP, PO-01A, PO-01B, PO-01B.1,
 * PO-02A, PO-02B, PO-02C, PO-02C.1, PO-02D1A, PO-02D1A.1, PO-02D1B, PO-02D2, PO-02D3 and PO-03A verifiers freeze.
 *
 * PO-03B changes three customer files, each narrowly. The Business Settings page (organization/page.tsx) loads the team
 * with an explicit five-field selection — id, name, e-mail, role, active — instead of every users column, and the Team
 * panel (team-panel.tsx) takes exactly that shape (TeamMember), so no password hash or MFA envelope is serialized to
 * the browser any more: the TFX security hotfix (branch fix/team-sensitive-fields-exposure), carried as its own commit.
 * The Team-change service (src/lib/team/member-changes.ts, a PO-03A file) now calls the shared customer-user mutation
 * service for its lock order, owner rules and status write — the same statements in the same order, the same messages.
 * It changes the two read-only PO-03A platform cores (primary-owners.ts, seat-accounting.ts — one batch read each, for a
 * directory page, display only) and the console: the Users page (now the operational directory), the company detail
 * (Manage users links to that company's users), the state table (user account active / disabled, the primary-owner
 * designation), the strings, the stylesheet (two layout classes), the error codes (three) and the permission list (two).
 * And it changes the two freeze verifiers (this layer's hooks). It adds eight files: the shared customer-user mutation
 * service (src/lib/team/customer-user-core.ts), the user read model and controls (src/lib/platform/), their server
 * actions, the users kit, the controls dialog, and the user page with its not-found. No schema module, SQL, migration,
 * seed, session, sign-in, registration, MFA or business file is in either list; seat limits are not enforced.
 *
 * The rule for an approved change is the one C8, ACC-01, the LCP stage and PO-01A…PO-03A used: no re-baseline. Each
 * changed file's hunks are recorded here byte for byte, [dca3362's text, PO-03B's text]; undone, the file is PO-03A's
 * (dca3362) to the byte (PO03B_BASE_SHA), so every older pin — PO-03A's added-file pins included — keeps its strength.
 * Each freeze verifier's PO-03B check proves the hunks are each file's only change and the added files are exactly as
 * recorded.
 *
 * Generated from the diff against PO03B_BASE (each hunk widened with context until it is unique in both files, its
 * dca3362 form nowhere in PO-03B's); changing a PO-03B file means regenerating this record, which is then part of the
 * change under review.
 */
